:: Upper_Lake_Mist_Start [#samayam:MADDHAMA_MIDNIGHT #flow:kandy_mist_bamboo #audio:monsoon_light #haptic:heartbeat_slow #vignette:0.50]
The last bus down to the Kandy clock tower left twenty minutes ago. Cold mist rolls off the black surface of the lake below, swallowing the curve of Upper Lake Road in a wet, chalky shroud.

To your left, the moss-slick stone retaining wall borders the giant bamboo thickets of Udawattakele Sanctuary. It is 11:46 PM. Around your right wrist, the white three-knotted Pirith Nula thread from the Dalada Maligawa feels damp against your pulse. Up ahead, the single municipal streetlamp flickers with {mutate: "a failing sodium bulb" -> "the pale yellow glow of a funeral oil wick" @2700}.

[[Walk briskly down the hill through the bamboo shadow->False_Tuk_Headlight][$taboo_walked_samayam = true, $tanikama += 10]]
[[Wait under the closed tin awning of the wayside tea stall->Three_Wheeler_Wait][$taboo_walked_samayam = true, $tanikama += 15]]


:: Three_Wheeler_Wait [#samayam:MADDHAMA_MIDNIGHT #flow:kandy_mist_bamboo #audio:monsoon_light #haptic:heartbeat_slow #vignette:0.56]
You step beneath the rusted tin awning. No three-wheeler engine echoes anywhere on the hill. The only sound is rainwater gurgling inside the stone culvert across the road and the dry clatter of giant bamboo stems knocking together in the wind.

From twenty paces up the dark lane, a woman's voice calls out softly through the fog—using {mutate: "a word you cannot quite catch" -> "the childhood nickname only your mother uses" @2400}.

[[Call back into the mist to ask who is there->Culvert_Whisper_Echo][$taboo_answered_call = true, $balma += 20]]
[[Keep your mouth shut, touch your Pirith Nula, and start walking down->False_Tuk_Headlight][@anchor_held $balma -= 5]]


:: Culvert_Whisper_Echo [#samayam:MADDHAMA_MIDNIGHT #flow:mohini_saree_silhouette #audio:ceb_power_cut #haptic:dread_throb #vignette:0.68 #balma:10]
The moment your voice leaves your lips, the echo does not bounce off the hillside—it answers from directly beneath your boots inside the storm drain.

Water sloshes against the stone grate, and pale fingers stained with milky tree-sap reach up through the iron bars, whispering: {mutate: "Help me lift my child out of the drain" -> "You gave me your voice at midnight; now lend me your arms" @2100}.

[[Wrench your heel back from the drain grate and run down the road->Bamboo_Culvert_Approach][$tanikama += 10]]
[[Hold the Pirith Nula tight and spit once onto the iron grate->Bamboo_Culvert_Approach][@anchor_held $balma -= 5]]


:: False_Tuk_Headlight [#samayam:MADDHAMA_MIDNIGHT #flow:kandy_mist_bamboo #audio:monsoon_heavy #haptic:heartbeat_slow #vignette:0.60]
Through the swirling fog behind you, a single yellow headlight sweeps around the bend. A black three-wheeler coasts slowly down the incline with its two-stroke engine strangely silent, rolling to a stop beside the bamboo wall.

Rain sheets off the canvas hood. From the shadowed passenger bench comes the faint rustle of wet white silk and {mutate: "the squeak of a vinyl seat" -> "a soft, rhythmic lullaby hummed through clenched teeth" @2300}.

[[Wave the three-wheeler down and climb into the dry backseat->Backseat_Wet_Saree][$balma += 20]]
[[Ignore the silent three-wheeler and climb the stone steps toward the forest edge->Sanctuary_Stone_Steps][$tanikama += 10]]
[[Keep walking along the asphalt road with your thumb on the Pirith Nula->Bamboo_Culvert_Approach][@anchor_held $balma -= 5]]


:: Backseat_Wet_Saree [#samayam:MADDHAMA_MIDNIGHT #flow:mohini_saree_silhouette #audio:ceb_power_cut #haptic:heartbeat_panic #vignette:0.78 #balma:15]
You duck under the canvas flap onto the vinyl bench—and freeze. The driver's seat in front of you is completely empty; the handlebars are rusted solid and wrapped in dead creeper vines.

Beside your left thigh, the seat cushion is soaking wet. A woman in a drenched white saree sits pressed against your shoulder in the dark cab, turning her pupil-less face toward your neck: {mutate: "You climbed in out of the rain on your own" -> "Hold the child while I pin my border, malli" @2000}.

[[Throw yourself backward out of the cab onto the wet asphalt->Bamboo_Culvert_Approach][$taboo_met_eyes = true, $balma += 15]]
[[Clamp your thumb onto the Pirith Nula and kick out through the canvas->Bamboo_Culvert_Approach][@anchor_held $balma -= 10]]


:: Sanctuary_Stone_Steps [#samayam:MADDHAMA_MIDNIGHT #flow:kaduru_puddle_feet #audio:monsoon_heavy #haptic:dread_throb #vignette:0.66]
You scramble up five mossy stone steps toward the locked iron gate of Udawattakele. Overhanging Kaduru trees drip thick, acrid white sap onto the stone.

When you look back down at the road, the three-wheeler is gone—only a rotting green banana trunk lies in the middle of the lane, while the weeping sound rises directly ahead of you at the culvert bend: {mutate: "wind whistling through the sanctuary wire" -> "a mother sobbing for someone to carry her cold bundle" @2300}.

[[Descend back to the road edge and approach the culvert bend->Bamboo_Culvert_Approach][$tanikama += 5]]


:: Bamboo_Culvert_Approach [#samayam:MADDHAMA_MIDNIGHT #flow:kandy_mist_bamboo #audio:monsoon_heavy #haptic:dread_throb #vignette:0.62]
As you round the hair-pin bend where the giant bamboo arches completely over the asphalt, the air turns thick with a sharp, cloying floral scent. It is not night-blooming jasmine; it is the bruised, milky sap of {mutate: "wet roadside weeds" -> "crushed Kaduru blossoms and camphor water" @2500}.

Sitting on the low concrete culvert parapet in the drizzle is a slender woman in a plain white saree. Her long black hair hangs soaking wet past her waist, and she rocks a small white cloth bundle against her shoulder, weeping softly.

[[Cross to the far gravel edge of the road to pass without disturbing her->Cross_Road_Verge][$tanikama += 5]]
[[Slow your pace and ask why she is sitting in the rain at midnight->Weeping_By_The_Wall][$taboo_answered_call = true, $balma += 15]]


:: Cross_Road_Verge [#samayam:MADDHAMA_MIDNIGHT #flow:mohini_saree_silhouette #audio:monsoon_heavy #haptic:heartbeat_slow #vignette:0.66]
You step toward the outer edge of the road, keeping your boots on the wet gravel. Before you can take three strides, the weeping stops.

Without the sound of a single footstep splashing in the runoff, she is standing directly in the center of the narrow lane five paces ahead of you. The white saree pleats hang loose and untidy, soaked translucent at the hem, and from inside the cloth bundle comes {mutate: "a muffled, rasping cough" -> "the high, breathless cry of a newborn infant" @2300}.

[[Lock your thumb on your Pirith Nula and keep your eyes fixed on the wet tar->Gaze_Down_Puddle][@anchor_held $balma -= 5]]
[[Raise your head to see why she is blocking the road->Look_Into_Her_Eyes][$taboo_met_eyes = true, $balma += 25]]


:: Weeping_By_The_Wall [#samayam:MADDHAMA_MIDNIGHT #flow:mohini_saree_silhouette #audio:monsoon_heavy #haptic:dread_throb #vignette:0.68 #balma:10]
She rises from the culvert stone as you speak. In the pale mist, her skin has the dull, waxen sheen of peeled manioc root. The white saree is draped without a brooch, its wet border slipping down from her left shoulder as the infant inside her bundle wails louder.

She steps into your path, shivering violently, and whispers: {mutate: "My husband went to fetch a three-wheeler near the lake" -> "You walked alone in Tanikama, and my child is so cold" @2400}.

[[Press your thumb to the Pirith Nula and drop your gaze to the rain puddle->Gaze_Down_Puddle][@anchor_held $balma -= 5]]
[[Look into her dark eyes to see if she is injured->Look_Into_Her_Eyes][$taboo_met_eyes = true, $balma += 25]]


:: Look_Into_Her_Eyes [#samayam:MADDHAMA_MIDNIGHT #flow:mohini_saree_silhouette #audio:ceb_power_cut #haptic:heartbeat_panic #vignette:0.78 #balma:15]
You meet her gaze. Her pupils are impossibly wide, swallowing the amber streetlamp reflection without throwing back a single spark of light. A sudden, dizzying warmth floods your chest, dulling the cold rain on your face.

With her left hand, she reaches up and slowly draws three wet strands of hair back across her cheek, her fingers curling in a slow, beckoning arc. Your own right hand {mutate: "hangs heavy at your side" -> "twitches upward to mirror her exact gesture" @2100}.

[[Raise your hand to brush the rain from your own forehead->The_Slipping_Saree_Plea][$taboo_mirrored_gesture = true, $balma += 20, $tanikama += 10]]
[[Force your fingers closed around the Pirith Nula thread on your wrist->The_Slipping_Saree_Plea][@anchor_held $balma -= 10]]


:: Gaze_Down_Puddle [#samayam:MADDHAMA_MIDNIGHT #flow:kaduru_puddle_feet #audio:monsoon_heavy #haptic:iron_grip #vignette:0.52]
You keep your chin tucked and your thumb pressed hard against the three knots of the Pirith Nula. On the black asphalt between you, a rainwater puddle catches the dim amber glow of the streetlamp.

Floating on the surface of the puddle are three bruised white Kaduru flowers. At the far edge of the water, the wet white hem of her saree sways—and beneath it, {mutate: "her bare heels rest in the mud" -> "there are no feet touching the wet stone at all" @2200}.

[[Step sideways toward the downhill slope without lifting your eyes->The_Slipping_Saree_Plea][$tanikama -= 5]]
[[Look up to see how she is floating above the road->The_Slipping_Saree_Plea][$taboo_met_eyes = true, $balma += 20]]


:: The_Slipping_Saree_Plea [#samayam:MADDHAMA_MIDNIGHT #flow:mohini_saree_silhouette #audio:ceb_power_cut #haptic:heartbeat_panic #vignette:0.80]
She glides half a step closer. The smell of wet burial cloth, crushed Kaduru sap, and sour milk fills your lungs until the mountain air feels unbreathable.

The white saree pleat slips further down her shoulder. With a soft sob, she holds the squirming, crying bundle out toward your chest with both hands: {mutate: "Ane malli, hold my baby for one second while I pin my saree" -> "Take my burden into your arms and give me your breath" @2200}.

[[Reach out with both hands to hold the crying infant for her->The_Infant_Drop_Trap][$taboo_accepted_bundle = true, $balma += 30]]
[[Keep your arms pinned to your sides and back away down the hill->The_Infant_Drop_Trap][$balma += 5]]


:: The_Infant_Drop_Trap [#samayam:MADDHAMA_MIDNIGHT #flow:mohini_saree_silhouette #audio:yak_bera_ritual #haptic:heartbeat_panic #vignette:0.88 #balma:15]
As you hesitate, her pale fingers suddenly open. She lets go of the bundle completely.

The white cloth drops straight toward the jagged stone edge of the culvert. In that split second of terror, your eyes see {mutate: "a helpless infant plunging toward the rock" -> "a rotting green banana stem wrapped in a funeral shroud" @1900}. If you release the Pirith Nula to catch it, the contract is sealed.

[[Keep the Pirith Nula held tight, stare at the puddle, and let it hit the stone->Outcome_Athura_Road_Escaped][@anchor_held $balma -= 30]]
[[Lunge forward and catch the falling bundle in your arms->Outcome_Athura_Mohini_Bound][$taboo_accepted_bundle = true, $balma += 40]]
[[Scream and cover your face with both hands->Outcome_Athura_Mohini_Bound][$taboo_mirrored_gesture = true, $balma += 30]]


:: Outcome_Athura_Road_Escaped [#samayam:ALUYA_DAWN #flow:kaduru_puddle_feet #audio:monsoon_light #haptic:iron_grip #vignette:0.35]
You lock your jaw and keep your thumb crushed against the sacred thread. The bundle strikes the asphalt with a dull, fibrous thud—not bone, but a waterlogged chunk of banana trunk that splits open in the puddle.

A shriek like tearing wet silk echoes up into the giant bamboo of Udawattakele. When the headlights of a morning bakery lorry sweep around the bend, the road is empty save for the split plantain stem and a scatter of black Kaduru seeds.

[[Examine the forensic case from the Kattadiya perspective->Kattadiya_Mohini_Entry][$tanikama = 40]]
[[Walk Upper Lake Road again from 11:46 PM->Upper_Lake_Mist_Start][$balma = 20, $tanikama = 50]]


:: Outcome_Athura_Mohini_Bound [#samayam:MADDHAMA_MIDNIGHT #flow:mohini_saree_silhouette #audio:yak_bera_ritual #haptic:dread_throb #vignette:0.90]
The moment the wet bundle touches your forearms, its weight turns to freezing lead. The Pirith Nula on your wrist snaps cleanly in two.

You look up—and there is no infant in your arms, and no woman before you, only tall jaws laughing down through a curtain of soaking black hair. A street-sweeper finds you at dawn curled beside the culvert, shivering with a burning fever, your arms locked rigidly in a cradle shape and your tongue unable to form a word.

[[Accept the Bulath Hurulla and step into the Kattadiya role->Kattadiya_Mohini_Entry][$tanikama = 80]]
[[Return to Upper Lake Road at 11:46 PM->Upper_Lake_Mist_Start][$balma = 20, $tanikama = 50]]


:: Kattadiya_Mohini_Entry [#samayam:MADDHAMA_MIDNIGHT #flow:sanni_mask_torch #audio:monsoon_light #haptic:iron_grip #vignette:0.46]
Two nights later, in a hillside house above Peradeniya, the young man sits propped against the wall. His arms remain locked at the elbows as if cradling an invisible weight, and whenever the rain hits the window, he smiles vacantly and whispers toward the doorway.

His father places the Bulath Hurulla sheaf before your brass pahana lamp. Without asking how they found him on the road, you lift the top betel leaf to the flame.

[[Pass the Pahana flame behind the betel leaf to read the road Lakunu->Sastra_Kaduru_Leaf_Check][$tanikama -= 5]]
[[Examine the patient's locked forearms and snapped wrist thread first->Patient_Catatonia_Inspection][$tanikama -= 5]]


:: Sastra_Kaduru_Leaf_Check [#samayam:MADDHAMA_MIDNIGHT #flow:sanni_mask_torch #audio:ceb_power_cut #haptic:heartbeat_slow #vignette:0.52]
Against the amber flame, the leaf reveals the signature of the lonely road: a pale milky film coats the right veins where mimetic gesture or spoken answers occurred, while a black rot eats the petiole base where the phantom bundle was accepted.

The veins confirm what the hospital doctors missed: {mutate: "the boy is suffering from exposure to the cold mountain rain" -> "Mala Mohini has bound his mind through the infant contract" @2400}.

[[Inspect the patient's physical symptoms in the room->Patient_Catatonia_Inspection][$balma += 5]]
[[Prepare the Three Kaduru-Wood Masks and Kesel Kanda stem->Three_Mask_Paliya_Prep][$balma += 10]]


:: Patient_Catatonia_Inspection [#samayam:MADDHAMA_MIDNIGHT #flow:kaduru_puddle_feet #audio:ceb_power_cut #haptic:heartbeat_slow #vignette:0.60]
You kneel beside the reed mat. Around his right wrist hangs the frayed end of a snapped Pirith Nula, stained grey with dried Kaduru sap. His eyes are dilated, fixed past your shoulder as though watching a woman in white standing by the door.

When you try to unbend his forearms, the tendons feel like cold iron. To unlock his grip, you cannot use brute force—you must stage the three-part Mohini Paliya theatre to externalize and shatter the illusion inside his mind.

[[Lay out the Three Masks and consecrated offerings->Three_Mask_Paliya_Prep][$tanikama -= 10]]
[[Re-verify the betel leaf veins against the brass lamp->Sastra_Kaduru_Leaf_Check][$tanikama -= 5]]


:: Three_Mask_Paliya_Prep [#samayam:MADDHAMA_MIDNIGHT #flow:sanni_mask_torch #audio:yak_bera_ritual #haptic:iron_grip #vignette:0.58]
In the courtyard beneath a temporary gokkola canopy, the yak bera drum begins its rolling cadence. Before the altar stand three carved Ambalangoda masks of Kaduru wood alongside a freshly cut green banana stem—the Kesel Kanda—wrapped in white cloth like an infant.

You dance the first two states in sequence: first the blandly alluring pink Coquette mask to draw the patient's gaze toward the arena; then the grotesquely swollen Pregnancy mask, groaning under a crushing burden until the boy shudders in revulsion. Now comes the final severance.

[[Don the third Maternal mask, place the Kesel Kanda at his feet, and raise the blade->Midnight_Kesel_Kanda_Severance][$balma += 10]]


:: Midnight_Kesel_Kanda_Severance [#samayam:MADDHAMA_MIDNIGHT #flow:sanni_mask_torch #audio:yak_bera_ritual #haptic:heartbeat_panic #vignette:0.84 #balma:15]
Dummala resin flashes gold against the mist. As you lay the wrapped banana stem before the patient's locked arms, the pahana flame bends flat and turns indigo. From the bamboo shadows beyond the compound wall, Mohini's voice pleads through the drumbeat: {mutate: "Do not strike the child, give him back to me" -> "By the warrant of Goddess Pattini and the Triple Gem, the false child is severed" @2100}.

You must hold the sacred ward to keep your blade true before slicing the surrogate bundle in half.

[[Hold the sacred ward, chant the Pattini Varama, and cleave the Kesel Kanda in two->Outcome_Kattadiya_Mohini_Cured][@anchor_held $balma = 0]]
[[Bring the plantain knife down without holding the sacred ward->Outcome_Kattadiya_Mohini_Failed][$balma += 35]]


:: Outcome_Kattadiya_Mohini_Cured [#samayam:ALUYA_DAWN #flow:kaduru_puddle_feet #audio:monsoon_light #haptic:iron_grip #vignette:0.32]
The blade shears cleanly through the white cloth and green banana trunk. Clear, watery sap spills across the reed mat. At that exact instant, the young man's locked forearms drop limp into his lap with a long, shuddering exhalation.

You dip a fresh three-stranded Pirith Nula into turmeric water, chant the protective gatha, and knot it tightly around his right wrist as the mist over the Kandy hills turns pale gold with dawn.

[[Replay Casefile 02 from Upper Lake Road at 11:46 PM->Upper_Lake_Mist_Start][$balma = 20, $tanikama = 50]]
[[Examine a new Bulath Hurulla sheaf in Kattadiya Mode->Kattadiya_Mohini_Entry][$balma = 25]]


:: Outcome_Kattadiya_Mohini_Failed [#samayam:MADDHAMA_MIDNIGHT #flow:mohini_saree_silhouette #audio:yak_bera_ritual #haptic:dread_throb #vignette:0.88]
Your thumb slips from the ward as the blade falls. Instead of splitting the banana stem, the knife glances off the stone floor in a shower of sparks, and the dummala torch hisses out in the drizzle.

The patient's eyes roll back, his arms locking tighter around the empty air as a sound like a weeping infant echoes from inside the house. You must re-consecrate the masks and repeat the Paliya sequence before daybreak.

[[Re-light the torch and reset the Three Masks->Three_Mask_Paliya_Prep][$balma = 40]]
[[Return to the Sastra betel leaf inspection->Kattadiya_Mohini_Entry][$balma = 30]]
